re dictated by the source material and which are your own proposed choices.\n\n4. Consequential assumptions and uncertainties. List the assumptions that would most affect the conclusion, for example whether caching of retrieved templates is permitted, whether the same hardware and same concurrency are held constant, whether BoT is charged with retrieval-store construction time or only with per-query lookup, whether single-query baselines are given the same output-token budget, and whether overheads are measured for the baselines as well. Also state any uncertainty about what \"inference time\" is meant to include.\n\nPlease do not produce the full experiment design yet. I wish to agree the approach and the assumptions first, then have the complete design, controls, analysis plan and feasibility discussion afterwards. Keep the report concrete and itemised; I value precision over breadth.", "required_handoff_stage": "plan", "approach_approved": false, "public_task": {"question": "Does the Buffer of Thoughts (BoT) framework increase inference time compared to conventional single-query reasoning methods including Expert and PAL across various benchmarks including Game of 24, MGSM and Checkmate-in-One?", "context": "Design an experiment that answers the question. The researcher can clarify source-supported setup details by topic. Do not claim that an experiment was run.", "environment": {"runtime": "bubblewrap", "network": "disabled", "repository": "/workspace", "python": "python3", "software_environment": "system Python; project dependencies not preinstalled", "datasets": [], "gpu_enabled": false, "cpu_affinity_count": 224, "note": "Successful exploratory commands are not proof of a completed experiment."}, "researcher_topics": ["neurips2024/96264/6:setup_7", "neurips2024/96264/6:setup_8", "neurips2024/96264/6:setup_9", "neurips2024/96264/6:setup_28", "neurips2024/96264/6:setup_29"], "question_budget": 6, "actor_step_budget": 60, "continue_after_initial_plan": false}}"}