nfirmation).", "A single LLM backend (pinned checkpoint or pinned API model version) is used for all three methods, so latency differences reflect the framework, not different base models.", "Primary comparison is strictly single-query (k=1) for all arms; any self-consistency/k-vote variant is secondary.", "Accuracy and latency are logged from the same runs on an identical, pre-registered item set (paired design)."], "uncertainties": ["Definition boundary of \"inference time\" (LLM tokens only vs whole pipeline incl. embedding, retrieval, sandbox execution, parsing, retries) -- largest threat to answer validity; my default is end-to-end wall-clock with component decomposition.", "Whether Expert and PAL are each applicable/reported on all three benchmarks, i.e. whether all nine method x benchmark cells are answerable (decision D1).", "Whether a reference CoT arm should be added (decision D2).", "Which latency statistic is authoritative -- median (my proposal), mean, or P90 tail -- must be fixed before measurement.", "Base model identity/version, decoding settings and retrieval-store configuration are entirely unspecified in the supplied material and remain open until retrieved from the source topics.", "Reproducibility of the paper's absolute timings is unknown: if their measurements used a batch API, different concurrency, or an unpinned model version, our absolute numbers will not be comparable and only within-run paired contrasts are defensible.", "API-side latency variance may dominate the paired effect if a hosted endpoint is used; interleaving and per-item medians mitigate but do not eliminate this.", "Whether MGSM must be run on the full 2,500 items or a stratified per-language subsample (cost vs precision, unresolved).", "Whether any compute/backend exists at all for a real run; the present sandbox has no model, no data, no dependencies and no network, so a live execution would require resources outside it."]}", "kind": "ActionEvent"}
