% margin infeasible**); n=96, \u03c3_d=0.35 \u2192 \u00b19.2% (5% infeasible); n=500, \u03c3_d=0.25/0.35 \u2192 \u00b12.8%/\u00b13.9% (5% feasible). This is what makes 500 MGSM items (not 96) the defensible default and forbids claiming a 5% equivalence on Game of 24.\n\n**Accuracy-calibrated margin arithmetic (illustrative grid, not paper facts).** Break-even latency ratio R\\* = Acc_BoT/Acc_base, the largest tolerated slowdown that leaves time-per-correct-answer unchanged: base 0.50 with +2/+5 pts \u2192 +4.0%/+10.0%; base 0.70 \u2192 +2.9%/+7.1%; base 0.90 \u2192 +2.2%/+5.6%; base 0.94 \u2192 +2.1%/+5.3%; base 0.97 \u2192 +2.1%/+3.0%. Near-ceiling suites therefore tolerate far less than 10% in cost-per-correct terms.\n\n**Amortisation break-even (A1/C, per your request).** N\\* = C_build / t_lookup, the item count at which amortised construction per item equals one lookup: C_build=300 s, t_lookup=0.02 s \u2192 N\\*=15,000; 1,800 s/0.02 s \u2192 90,000; 1,800 s/0.005 s \u2192 360,000; 7,200 s/0.10 s \u2192 72,000. All benchmark suites here are \u22642,500 items, i.e. far below every N\\*. At N=596 the amortised construction charge is 0.50\u201312.1 s per item versus a 0.005\u20130.10 s lookup \u2014 **one to three orders of magnitude larger**. The cached convention therefore materially favours BoT, and must be reported alongside the cold-start variant rather than assumed away.\n\n**Budget arithmetic (12 cells = 9 required + 3 CoT reference; 1,096 items; R=5; +20 warm-up/cell).** 65,760 measured generations, 66,960 including warm-up. Sequential timed wall-clock: 37 h at 2 s/call, 93 h at 5 s, 186 h at 10 s, 372 h at 20 s. Completion tokens \u224819.7 M at 300 tok/call, 39.5 M at 600 tok/call.", "answer": "# Experiment design: does Buffer of Thoughts increase inference time relative to Expert prompting and PAL?\n\n**Standing statement.** Nothing here was executed. This is a design only; no outcome, direction or magnitude is asserted for any arm on any benchmark. Ever